= Levi's crisis.

With the victory of the Left Social Democrats, Paul Levi has promised to potentially abstain from government participation, maintain a strict course of opposition, refuse to cooperate with bourgeois parties, form grassroots ties with the KPD, and adopt a leftist program in order to satisfy the rank-and-file, which is dominated by a radical current. However, at the same time, Levi faces a growing sense of danger from the old guard, who are preparing to remove him and actively searching for any pretext to do so. Navigating this crisis will require Levi to buy the time, strike the ideal balance and eventually tighten his grip over the party.

- @demands: Grassroots, whom we rely on, forward their demands.

@demands

Grassroots demand the following to be done by the end of the year:

• We must declare the bourgeois as the primary enemy.
• We should abstain from usage of the radio or if it was done, broadcast radical message.
• Left Social Democrats must maintain dominance in the party.
• Reconcile with Communist Party and expel the right wing members such as Noske.
• Initiate at least two rallies for class struggle.
• Waive away party dues for unemployed members.
• Expel reformists from the party.
• Abstain from entering the government.

Depending on the situation, this list may expand. Failing all but one task will lead to heavy dissent from grassroots and they may move against us. At the same time, right wing factions consolidating and being angered by our actions will likely lead to coup from them.

- @root: Arise worker, arise against your bureaucrat.